{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/DevOps Agent Evaluation Criteria.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/DevOps Agent Evaluation Criteria.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"dev ops agent evaluation criteria dev ops agent evaluation criteria","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/DevOps Agent Evaluation Criteria.md","fileName":"DevOps Agent Evaluation Criteria.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"DevOps Agent Evaluation Criteria","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-27 12:11\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[AI Agent Observability and Evaluation]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["AI Agent Observability and Evaluation","agenticaifordevopsengineers.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/DevOps Agent Evaluation Criteria.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/DevOps Agent Evaluation Criteria.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"dev ops agent evaluation criteria dev ops agent evaluation criteria","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/DevOps Agent Evaluation Criteria.md","fileName":"DevOps Agent Evaluation Criteria.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"DevOps Agent Evaluation Criteria","heading":"DevOps Agent Evaluation Criteria","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"DevOps agent evaluation covers task adherence, tool correctness, output quality, safety, operational efficiency, and human usefulness. It asks whether the agent followed its instructions, selected the right tool with valid arguments, produced actionable grounded output, avoided policy violations, and used acceptable time and tokens.\n\nNo single score captures all of these dimensions. A structurally complete incident report may still recommend an unsupported action, while a safe response may be too vague to help. Evaluation should preserve individual checks so failures point to a specific behavior that can be improved.","ta